    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d510">

                <pb facs="0933" n="901" sameAs="frus:frus1958-60v06/pg901"/>

                <head>510. Diary Entry by the President, April 25, 1960<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d510-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1960-04-25"><hi rendition="#italic">April 25,
                        1960</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p>[Here follow entries unrelated to Cuba.]</p>
                <p>A little later Mr. Pawley came in to see me about our
                    relationships with Cuba.<anchor n="2" xml:id="d510-f2"/> He is very
                    knowledgeable in this area and since he has divested himself of his commercial
                    interests in the Latin American area, I find it profitable to talk with him. He
                    seems to think that a modicum of sense is not [<hi rendition="#italic"
                    >now</hi>?] characterizing some of Castro’s grandiose programs and plans. He
                    believes, as does Harry Guggenheim, that our relationship
                    with the whole of Latin America would be much improved if we should appoint an
                    Under Secretary with duties confined to this hemisphere. I brought up this idea
                    to the State Department many times over the past few years—the staffs there are
                    always so bitterly opposed that I am becoming quite sure that I am right. This
                    morning I told Secretary Herter<anchor
                        n="3" xml:id="d510-f3"/> that if I was to be put off in this matter again, I
                    wanted to have some very convincing reason.</p>
                <p>[Here follow entries unrelated to Cuba.]</p>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d510-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d510-f1-content">
                <p>Source: Eisenhower Library, Whitman File, DDE Diaries. The source text bears the
                    following note: “Dictated by DDE.”</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d510-f2" n="2" xml:id="d510-f2-content">
                <p>The President met with Pawley, 9: 14–9: 34 a.m. (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >ibid</hi>., President’s Daily Appointments)</p>
            </note>
            <note corresp="#d510-f3" n="3" xml:id="d510-f3-content">
                <p>Apparently a reference to the President’s meeting with Herter and Goodpaster, 11: 25–11: 32 a.m. (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >ibid</hi>.) No record of this meeting has been found.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
